notes={
365508:('parked_after_exact_search','Galvin–Marmorino Conjecture 6.2 and the actual Cambie–Goedgebeur–Jooken arXiv:2311.00075 Conjecture 1.1 inspected. Complement formulation: an (n-d-1)-regular graph should maximize clique count with as many K_(n-d) components as possible. All admissible labelled regular complements at orders 2 through 9 were enumerated; clique counts include the empty clique. Structured and unrestricted maxima agree for every pair. This checks existence of a structured maximizer, not uniqueness of all maximizers.','A general extremal transformation preserving regularity, or an unstructured graph beating the exact optimum over all allowed H. No such graph or transformation found.'),
365514:('excluded_prior_claim_and_paraphrase_defect','Primary Conjecture 1.2 of Kaur–Kumar arXiv:2608.08997 and its Theorem 1.4 already claim the complete cyclotomic criterion. The odd-k clause in the MathDB record incorrectly says irreducible and omits the even-i qualification. The intended criterion has a prior public claimed proof; this pass does not certify that proof. No novelty is available from repairing the paraphrase.','No new claim. Independently validating the 2026 claimed proof would be a separate audit, not a new solution of this record.'),
365604:('parked_prior_partial_resolution','Both versions of Bartoli–Pal–Stanica–Toccotelli inspected around the conjecture and resolution. Version 1 cites Bartoli–Timpanella 2022 for non-APN at m >= 20 plus earlier computations and proves non-permutation for m >= 25. Current version Theorem 6.3 states odd m >= 23; this is not the full m > 3 statement. The large-field source proof is algebraic-geometric, not a small literal finite certificate. No independent new finite-field computation was run on already tested degrees.','An exact all-u treatment of the remaining small odd degrees outside the published theorem, with a careful reconciliation of the source computational range and u restrictions. A bound improvement by a few source estimates would not meet the novelty standard.'),
365677:('parked_after_random_profiles','Current Conjecture 1, Definition 2, lower-bound discussion and earlier versions inspected. Undominated means strictly fewer than alpha of the voters put each outside candidate above every committee member. Ran 300 independent seeded random complete-ranking profiles for each c=4..10 and voter count 9,21,51 (6300 profiles). For each profile enumerated every size-2 committee and every opposing candidate. None had minimum worst domination strictly greater than 2/3. Endpoint-equality failures were not promoted. A few good choices (2506.22133) was located in search; HTML returned 404 and its body is unread.','A genuinely new election with a strict gap above 2/(k+1), or a full general existence proof. Random profiles are far from the structured lower-bound regimes, and do not certify any universal bound.'),
365771:('parked_deep_number_theory','O’Bryant source Conjecture 2 and dataset discussion inspected in both versions. The golden-ratio exponent is a finite explicit sum-product assertion, distinct from the asymptotic Erdos conjecture. Source data cannot count as a new counterexample. Current search found Omega solutions to OTHER questions in this source (golden minimizers and the seven-point real cell); these do not resolve the reserved integer exponent statement. No qualifying mechanism found; no source-dataset search run.','A new positive-integer set violating the golden exponent, independent of the source examples, or a uniform substantial sum-product inequality. Existing approximately 4/3-exponent technology does not immediately give the proposed exponent.'),
365865:('parked_flagship_structural','Topological cliques in sparse expanders, Conjecture 1.1 and introductory results inspected. This is the classical chromatic clique-immersion conjecture, not merely a new 2024 finite graph guess. Source states t <= 7 is known and t >= 8 is open; later sparse-expander asymptotic theorems have extra hypotheses. No small certified obstruction route identified.','A chromatic-critical graph with no K_t immersion for t >= 8, or a full structural theorem. Tiny graph sweeps within the known range would add no credit.'),
366050:('parked_topological_not_finite','Ends and end cohomology, Section 9 Conjecture 2, its neighbouring tree existence conjecture and suggested Tietze extension approach inspected in both versions. A tree means a locally finite acyclic simplicial 1-complex; proper maps and injective end maps are topological, not ordinary finite graph retractions. The source already suggests finite-tree extension followed by a proper exhaustion.','A compatible exhaustion/extension construction whose inverse images of compact subtrees are compact, or a noncompact generalized continuum obstructing that. Finite graph enumeration cannot test this quantifier.'),
366223:('parked_partial_source_resolution_analytic','Lin–Ma primary Conjecture 1 and Theorem 1.2 inspected. The source itself supplies the classification for k >= 3 and explicitly leaves k=2 open because of a priori estimates. Repeating the printed classification is not a new resolution; changing signs or normalization is not eligible. No finite route identified.','The missing k=2 a priori estimates and classification for the intended positive extremals in the remaining parameter range. No new PDE argument supplied.'),
366414:('excluded_source_refuted','Chapelier-Laget–Fromentin Section 2 explicitly refutes this very conjecture at type A_11, the next case after the old n <= 10 verification. Figure 8 and the coefficient discussion were inspected. Their computations through n=17 report only n=3 and n=11 failing. Our independent compact DP negative control at S_12 also detects failure.','None for discovery: reproducing the published counterexample or formalizing it earns zero credit.'),
366415:('parked_after_extended_exact_dp','Primary Conjecture 1.2 and Section 3 table inspected. Developed exact subset DP for the inversion graph with edges (i,j) for j-i congruent to 1 mod k. Full DP covers S_N for 2 <= N <= 21 and 3 <= k <= N. Compact palindrome DP extends to 22 <= N <= 24 and 3 <= k <= 24. All distributions are unimodal. For k >= N only adjacent inversions occur, so higher k add no new polynomial. Thus all k >= 3 are covered through type A_23. This goes beyond the source Section 3 table through n=12. Histograms sum to N! and match direct permutation enumeration through S_8.','A proof of unimodality for all n,k, or a first exact coefficient descent before the midpoint outside this range. The DP is diagnostic; no finite range theorem is submitted as the universal Lean endpoint.'),
366453:('excluded_prior_public_lean_development','Current Omega head 6aabd0ef13314679f92b922143be5084c054f1f9 contains D5/S3/Combinatorics/YoungFibonacci/PetrovScottMultiplicityDominance.lean and its blueprint. Both were fetched by pinned raw URL and read. Last path commit 17405edc663ecd04295edd2d5f1597a3d225a1fa is dated 2026-11-04T23:46:59Z, preceding this lane. Its public result addresses multiplicity support, equal hike, dominance and triangularity. It explicitly retains the printed odd-length splitB and disclaims the corrected matrix/Figure 8; an escape audit is unfinished. This is prior public work, not independently rechecked here.','No new discovery claim. Corrected source formulas versus fixed-weight formal definitions remain a fidelity issue; resolving a formula correction would not earn new-result credit.'),
366455:('parked_asymptotic_ramsey','Conlon–Fox–Pham–Yepremyan arXiv:2412.21194 Section 5 Conjecture 5.1 inspected. The desired constant is uniform in dimension; a successful coloring for a fixed n cannot settle the conjecture. Source distinguishes F_2^n from fields with characteristic 1 mod 4, where its nonuniform Cayley construction succeeds. Search found off-diagonal vector-space Ramsey progress, not a full direct resolution.','A uniform dimension-dependent coloring with linear monochromatic-size bound, or an obstruction ruling out every C. Small colorings do not furnish a finite counterexample to this existence asymptotic claim.'),
382287:('parked_source_construction_bridge_risk','Source Conjecture 5.1, fan-bouquet definition FB(s)=(s P3) join K1, Theorems 2.1–2.3, and examples around Figures 1–2 inspected. Here r FB(s) means r disjoint copies with one global bijective edge labeling. The source already reblocks a 5 by 2k labeling matrix to solve r arbitrary with even s, and cites odd r,s. A regrouping of these printed columns is exactly the kind of short source-construction augmentation excluded by the task. Citing 2025 tripartite and join papers were located; not all their bodies were read. Distinct from the accepted full-tree family, but not novelty-cleared.','A genuinely distinct full even-r, odd-s construction and a literature/body check against the extensive matrix-labeling family. No new construction or lower-bound obstruction supplied; no small arbitrary labeling search claimed.'),
382332:('parked_after_coil_gridding_search','Bevan et al. current and v1 Definition 3.9, Lemma 5.2, Conjecture 5.3 and Figure 10 examples inspected textually. Generated coil orders from C1–C4 as precedence constraints within each column/row, then independently enumerated integer gridding cuts and tested signed monotonicity. Tested all 16 choices of row/column orientations in the canonical 2 by 2 cycle at lengths 9..12 (64 cases), all 64 orientations in canonical 3 by 3 cycles at lengths 13..16 (256 cases), and all 64 orientations times 6 column orders times 6 row orders at length 13 (2304 cases, overlap retained). Every generated permutation had exactly one gridding. No cone/gluing of the length-8 printed example was proposed.','A structural proof at 2 ell+1 for arbitrary cyclic partial multiplication matrices, or a genuinely new larger-cycle failure. This search does not cover all ell >= 8, and geometric generation/completeness is not formalized.'),
357185:('parked_analytic_ground_state_gap','Meng source Conjecture 2.6, discussion distinguishing it from weak Conjecture 2.7, and Theorem 2.11 inspected. The source only proves an error estimate of order alpha^2/c^4, not exact equality. Older failures of max-min attainment do not automatically refute equality of the energy levels in this reserved statement.','A proof or strict separation of the two exact energies under the source parameter assumptions. No finite literal certificate route found; no surrogate weak-energy endpoint created.'),
357250:('excluded_literal_odd_length_defect_intended_even_scope_parked','Published Mol–Rampersad–Shallit Conjecture 6.5 was fetched and read, along with available arXiv versions. Its i=0 branch includes odd lengths 2^k-1, impossible for any Dyck word. That is a zero-credit source endpoint defect, not a new mathematical refutation. For the intended positive even lengths, enumerated all Dyck intervals of length <=4096 inside a prefix of 262144 terms of the regular paperfolding word using a running-height stack. All observed lengths have form 2^k-2^i with i>=1; every such length <=4096 occurs in that prefix. Complement orientation was tested separately and has other lengths, so changing the encoding would be a different statement.','For the intended corrected even statement, derive a full automaton or an induction on paperfolding heights and prove completeness for all starting positions. No new theorem claimed from correcting i=0.'),
357335:('parked_after_exact_sat_instance','Debski et al. Definition of strongly proper paths (every at most three consecutive edges rainbow), Theorems 1–3, Conjecture 10 and printed lower-bound family inspected. Built a complete SAT encoding for 3-color strongly proper connection on K_(3,6), enumerating all simple paths and their 3-periodic color patterns. It is satisfiable. The returned edge coloring was independently verified by direct simple-path search for every unordered vertex pair. No modification of the printed 2-connected G_d obstruction was promoted.','A general proof for 3-connected graphs or a 3-connected obstruction whose noncolorability is certified with literal path semantics. This single complete bipartite instance does not establish the full conjecture.'),
357415:('excluded_prior_published_resolution','Choi–Gan, The Ungar Game Played on Various Lattices, MIT PRIMES 2024 primary manuscript, Theorem 1.1 and Corollary 1.2 explicitly settle Defant–Kravitz–Williams Conjecture 6.1 with exactly f_(r-2)+(-1)^r. The 2025 JMM abstract also announces this settlement. Primary PDF retained and text extracted.','None for discovery. Formalizing the existing recurrence or Eeta-win classification would be known-result formalization.'),
357483:('parked_infinite_dynamics','Source Conjecture 1.1, its reference to Theorem 1.4, and the separate expander low-temperature bottleneck theorem inspected in both versions. The question extends adversarial nonconvergence from mean field; existing expander resistance to phase flipping is a different assertion, not an immediate counterexample. MathDB omits necessary theorem context.','A uniform adversarial corrupted-set strategy satisfying the actual Theorem 1.4 quantitative conclusion on expanders, or a source-scope obstruction. A finite equilibrium or one finite trajectory cannot resolve the asymptotic quantifier.'),
357530:('parked_spectral_geometry','Vu Spectral inequality for Dirac right triangles, introduction, area/perimeter conjecture and partial geometric bounds inspected. This concerns the lowest positive infinite-mass Dirac eigenvalue, not the Dirichlet Laplacian eigenvalue. Source only handles additional geometric hypotheses.','A full comparison of Dirac quadratic forms for all aspect ratios and all masses under each constraint, or a rigorous spectral separation certificate. No finite exact mechanism identified.')}
